# 2026-09-24 Phase 12.5: the one additional 'workbench agent run' authorized after items 1-5, to confirm the fixes did not break the chain.
# Single chain demo, not an evaluation (单次链路演示，不构成评测). Code at commit f135189 (items 1-5 of Phase 12.5).
# machine: Claude Code cloud container (Linux x86_64, no GPU). Key read from DEEPSEEK_API_KEY by name; never printed.
# scenario: official e_commerce_33 (AgentWorldModel-1K revision dde80a0, CC-BY-4.0), task index 0, request = task text verbatim

## configuration (process environment only; no .env file; budget and max_tokens left at their defaults)
PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=$PWD/.cache/pycache
WORKBENCH_LLM__BACKEND=openai_compat
WORKBENCH_LLM__BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
WORKBENCH_LLM__MODEL=deepseek-flash              # DeepSeek default thinking mode left unchanged
WORKBENCH_LLM__API_KEY_ENV=DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
# no WORKBENCH_LLM__MAX_TOKENS / WORKBENCH_AGENT__TOKEN_BUDGET: defaults 8192 / 240000 (ADR-018)
WORKBENCH_ENV__RUNS_DIR=data/p125/runs
WORKBENCH_GATEWAY__AUDIT_PATH=data/p125/audit.jsonl
WORKBENCH_AGENT__CHECKPOINT_DB=data/p125/checkpoints.sqlite
WORKBENCH_AGENT__MEMORY_DB=data/p125/memory.sqlite

## pre-run checks (free): DEEPSEEK_API_KEY present (existence only); `workbench doctor` llm: https://api.deepseek.com/models reachable

## command
$ time uv run workbench agent run "<e_commerce_33 task 0>" --scenario e_commerce_33 --approve auto --approver claude-code-operator
# approval: decided in advance by the operator (Claude Code) for this demo; the gate itself still pauses the graph,
# records approval_requested/approval_granted and issues a one-time token for each write call.

