## what this run shows about each Phase 12.5 fix (engineering observations from this one run; not an evaluation)
# item 1 (ADR-015): both write tools the model called were already graded write by name and needed approval:
#   get_or_create_active_cart is a GET route, graded write by its verb 'create' (source heuristic; the floor
#   does not apply to GET); add_item_to_cart is POST, verb 'add' => write, floor write (no change).
#   Checked with workbench.gateway.policy.classify + workbench.envs.catalog.load_route_methods on data/awm1k.
# item 2 (ADR-016): the audit summaries keep the microsecond timestamp '2026-09-24T18:37:39.267449'; '[PHONE]' occurs 0 times
#   (Phase 12: the same field became '2026-09-24T17:05:[PHONE]').
# item 3 (ADR-017): act calls 2-5 carried native tools and earlier assistant turns and none failed: an LLM error
#   (for example HTTP 400) would end the run with a 'terminated' event, reason llm_error (agent/nodes/act.py:20-24);
#   this trace has none and termination is None (event types: session_created 1, node 8, llm 6, tool_call 4,
#   approval_requested 2, approval_granted 2, memory_saved 2, final 1). Whether reasoning_content was attached is not
#   recorded in the trace, and DeepSeek also returned 200 without it in Phase 12 (LIMITATIONS §6), so this run cannot
#   show the pass-back itself; the unit tests do (tests/unit/test_llm_reasoning.py).
# item 4 (ADR-018): tokens per act call 14515, 15512, 16100, 16289, 16675 (Phase 12: 25764, 26615, 27403, 27741);
#   plan 12586; tokens_used 93736 with the default budget 240000 and default max_tokens 8192 (no overrides).
# item 5 (ADR-019): the official e_commerce_33 server was started with the allowlisted environment and served all 39 tools.

